---
import ReferenceTable from '../../components/ReferenceTable.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import DocumentLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.contribute;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<DocumentLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <ContentCard>
<p class="section-kicker">Questions, layers, implementations, and review</p>
    <h2>Contribution types</h2>
    <ReferenceTable label="Contribution types"><thead><tr><th>Contribution</th><th>Useful content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Question or profile review</td><td>A defined investigation need, evidence criteria, supported and unresolved examples, and source references.</td></tr><tr><td>Vendor or organization graph</td><td>Layer ownership, public dependencies, additional meaning, example files, and validation results.</td></tr><tr><td>Implementation report</td><td>Supported roles, binding versions, named checks, cross-tool exchange results, and known losses.</td></tr><tr><td>Standards mapping</td><td>Versioned source and target objects, property-level mappings, assumptions, and round-trip examples.</td></tr><tr><td>Technical finding</td><td>An exact requirement or artifact reference, a minimal counterexample, and observed versus expected behavior.</td></tr></tbody></ReferenceTable>
    <div class="cta-group"><Button variant="primary" href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/issues/new?template=implementation-report.yml">Implementation report</Button><Button variant="secondary" href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/issues/new?template=core-rfc.yml">Change proposal</Button></div>
    <h2>Proposal contents</h2>
    <ol><li>Artifact identity and version, the problem, and expected behavior.</li><li>A minimal illustrative example, with successful and failing cases where relevant.</li><li>Compatibility, privacy, and security effects and alternatives considered.</li><li>Affected Core requirements or binding rules, check results, and untested scope.</li><li>Source attribution, relevant affiliations, and conflicts.</li></ol>
    <h2>Case material</h2>
    <p>Public fixtures use fictional or authorized, de-identified material. Confidential investigation records and credentials belong outside public issues. A public standard does not require public disclosure of case evidence. Vulnerabilities use the repository's <a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/security/advisories/new">private reporting channel</a>.</p>
    <h2>Review process</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/docs/review-process.md">finding process</a> records observations, responses, objections, and disposition. Proposed formal governance is described separately in <a href="/governance/">Governance</a>. A repository merge records a project change rather than certification or a governance appointment.</p>
    <p><a href="/review/">Pinned technical review package</a> · <a href="/graphs/coverage/">Question review ledger</a> · <a href="/extensions/">Graph layering guide</a> · <a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/pulls">Code and proposals</a></p>
  </ContentCard>
</DocumentLayout>
